cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FlyMog
message: >-
  FlyMog is an entertainment project. If you use the code, cite it as software.
  The scientific work it builds on is listed under references and must be cited
  separately.
type: software
authors:
  - name: FlyMog contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/FokantRazgul/FlyMogBot"
license: MIT

references:
  # --- Visual front end -----------------------------------------------------
  - type: software
    title: flyvis
    repository-code: "https://github.com/TuragaLab/flyvis"
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      Verified: MIT license classifier in the package's pyproject.toml, version
      1.2.0 on PyPI, requires Python >=3.9,<3.13. Ships a connectome of 65 optic
      lobe cell types with 8 input units and 34 output units.
    authors:
      - name: Turaga Lab

  - type: article
    title: >-
      Connectome-constrained networks predict neural activity across the fly
      visual system
    journal: Nature
    year: 2024
    notes: >-
      Lappalainen et al. The model implemented by flyvis.
      TODO(verify) full author list, volume, pages and DOI against the
      publisher; only the existence of the paper has been confirmed.
    authors:
      - name: "TODO(verify) full author list"

  # --- Central brain model --------------------------------------------------
  - type: software
    title: Drosophila brain model
    repository-code: "https://github.com/philshiu/Drosophila_brain_model"
    license: MIT
    year: 2023
    notes: >-
      Verified by reading the repository: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023
      Philip Shiu and Nico Spiller. Source of the leaky integrate-and-fire
      parameters in configs/sim.yaml and of the FlyWire v783 connectivity
      distribution used here.
    authors:
      - name: Philip Shiu
      - name: Nico Spiller

  # --- Sources of the individual LIF parameters -----------------------------
  # These are the works the reference implementation cites for each value.
  # The DOIs are transcribed from its default_params block.
  - type: article
    title: Ring attractor dynamics emerge from a spiking model of the entire protocerebral bridge
    doi: 10.3389/fnbeh.2017.00008
    year: 2017
    notes: >-
      Cited by the reference model for the resting, reset and threshold
      potentials and the membrane time constant. TODO(verify) the title and
      author list against the publisher; the DOI is transcribed from the code.
    authors:
      - name: Kakaria
      - name: de Bivort

  - type: article
    doi: 10.1088/2634-4386/ac3ba6
    title: "TODO(verify) title"
    notes: >-
      Cited by the reference model for the synaptic time constant of 5 ms.
    authors:
      - name: "Jürgensen et al. TODO(verify)"

  - type: article
    doi: 10.7554/eLife.62362
    title: "TODO(verify) title"
    notes: >-
      Cited by the reference model for the refractory period of 2.2 ms.
    authors:
      - name: "Lazar et al. TODO(verify)"

  - type: article
    doi: 10.3389/fncel.2015.00029
    title: "TODO(verify) title"
    year: 2015
    notes: >-
      Cited by the reference model for the synaptic delay of 1.8 ms.
    authors:
      - name: "Paul et al. TODO(verify)"

  # --- Connectome and annotations -------------------------------------------
  - type: generic
    title: FlyWire FAFB adult Drosophila brain connectome and annotations
    notes: >-
      The annotation repository flyconnectome/flywire_annotations asks, in its
      README, that users cite Berg et al. (2025), Schlegel et al. (2024),
      Matsliah et al. (2024) and Dorkenwald et al. (2024). That request is
      verified; the bibliographic details of those four papers are not.
      TODO(verify) each before citing, and see docs/DATA_LICENSES.md for the
      unresolved license question.
    authors:
